Message-ID: <SE2KEXCH019HF4slym2000004f8@se2kexch01.insightful.com>

>Hi,
>
>I am a newbie to splus, I am wondering if it is possible to output the 
>simulated samples(it is a time series, but could be other data as well) from 
>bootstrap function, ie, if I run 1000 times, I'd like to get those 1000 sets 
>of simulated samples out in some readable format(text for example), so that 
>I can play with the numbers.
>
>thanks in advance.
>
>Mike

First, install the S+Resample library (URL below).
Then suppose you've created a bootstrap object, using e.g.:
        boot <- bootstrap(x, mean)
        boot <- bootstrap(x, mean, save.indices = T)
Then you can use
        indices _ resampGetIndices(boot)
to extract a matrix of the resampling indices.  Then,
        x[ indices[ , 30] ]
contains the data used in the 30th bootstrap sample.

Couple of additional notes:
* The use of save.indices=T is optional; it speeds up resampGetIndices
  and some additional later calculations.
* For bootstrapping time series, you may wish to use e.g.:
        sampler = samp.blockBootstrap(blockLength = 20)
when calling bootstrap() (the 20 should be replaced with an appropriate
block length).

