Lucke, Joseph F wrote:
> The easiest way is  lm(post-pre ~ treatment, data=GLU).

This method is not appropriate in my opinion, as it does not adjust for 
pre.  See Stephen Senn's book Statistical Issues in Drug Development. 
And if you are going to (properly) adjust for pre there is no advantage 
to analyzing post-pre instead of post, and a disadvantage in terms of 
having to explain why pre appears 2 places in the model.

Frank Harrell

