Barlas, Suna wrote:
> I think a linear mixed model would be most suitable here. I have never
> been a fan of "change from baseline" analysis or analysis of covariance
> where baseline is one of the covariates in the model for several reasons.
>
>
> Suna Barlas

Change from baseline is usually a disaster (due to measurement error, 
regression to the mean, floor and ceiling effects, interpretability) but 
analysis of covariance is a superior approach.  A linear mixed model 
when there is only one "post" measurement is not advisable.

Frank Harrell

