On Sat, 5 Jun 2004, shahab einabadi wrote:

> How can I make a 50000*50000 matrix
> on 
> Intel Pentium 4  processor
> 2000 MHz
>  Win XP

Well, that is 2.5billion entries and you have a 32bit processor with a
per-process address space of 2Gb under your OS (or perhaps 3Gb if you
tweak it).  And S matrices have a minimum of 4 bytes per entry, AFAIK so 
you need close to 10Gb.

So I think the more pertinent question is `is it possible to make a 
50000*50000 matrix on a 32bit OS in S', and the answer is no.

