     1.  I don't think "step" tries all possible combinations of 
variables.  I have not studied the documentation recently, but I would 
expect it to, e.g., start with a null model (y ~ 1), and iterate, 
looking for variables to add or delete from the model. 

     2.  You may also wish to consider "stepAIC" in library(MASS). 

     3.  To check Prof. Harrell's point, it may be wise to run a few 
simulations, e.g. replacing your response variable with random 
permutations thereof and see what the algorithm says is the best model.  
A few months ago, I did this with my own tailored stepwise regression 
and found a huge bias towards selecting something from among 
uncorrelated sets of pseudo-random numbers. 

     hope this helps.  spencer graves

