This was suggested as a way to compute row variances:
>rowVars <- function(x, ...) {
>  n <- NCOL(x)
>  (rowSums(x^2, ...) - n * rowMeans(x, ...)^2)/(n - 1)
>}

That would be subject to large roundoff error, and can even give negative
variances.  No reputable statistical software would compute variance
that way (though Excel does).

In contrast, the calculations inside S-PLUS var(), rowVars(), & colVars()
are highly accurate -- taking squares only after subtracting the 
mean, computing all sums hierarchically to reduce roundoff error,
and performing an additional correction.  See help(var).

Tim Hesterberg

