From andy_liaw at merck.com  Tue Jun  8 12:40:14 2004
From: andy_liaw at merck.com (Liaw, Andy)
Date: Tue, 08 Jun 2004 08:40:14 -0400
Subject: Re: Variable Expressions
In-Reply-To: <5.2.1.1.2.20040607211627.02717d68@127.0.0.1>
Message-ID: <3A822319EB35174CA3714066D590DCD504AF7E4E@usrymx25.merck.com>

Spencer has shown one way, using eval() on strings coerced into expressions.
One other alternative is to use assign():

for (i in seq(along=objname)) {
    assign(objname[i], read.table(filename[i], ...))
}

or even something like:

datList <- lapply(filename, read.table, ...)
names(datList) <- objname

HTH,
Andy

