From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Fri Jun 25 20:26:11 2004
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Fri, 25 Jun 2004 21:26:11 +0100
Subject: Re: AICc and LME
In-Reply-To: <002501c45af0$78d93c10$d4ad8081@ces>
References: <002501c45af0$78d93c10$d4ad8081@ces>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.44.0406252117200.5755-100000@gannet.stats>

I am afraid neither AIC nor AICc are valid for mixed-effects models.
They assume IID observations (or something close to it like an AR series 
with IID innovations) and that the parameter space is open (not true for 
variance-component parameters).  

What to use for model selection in LME models is a research topic.  
